Personally, with around 700 games in (this
Nth incarnation of) my logfile, I'm having similar
issues.  I'd like a record file sized big enough to
reserve 100 entries at a time for each
class/race/alignment combination.  [How many 100s
would that make total?] That way, I'd have the last
100 tries playing any one combination against which
to compare my current (twisted) efforts.

Like the OP, I find it more than a bit frustrating
that my play over many years has produced a record
file into which I can now almost never any more
insert an entry at the end of a game, because of so
many outlier good games cluttering up the record
file compared to my general run of really, really
bad games.

So, also, I'd like an easy way to dump out of the
record file the bottom half of each combination's
100 entry bin, just to make room to add more current
fairly awful game scores when it becomes overly hard
to do so.

The issue of how on earth sensibly to _display_ the
current games score in that much larger context so
as to present a meaningful comparison to the player,
is left as an exercise for the patch writer.

